            }); While pondering Savage Buffalo Spirit Megaways from developer BGaming, some interesting info from the Internet arose. Despite buffalo or bison, as they are also known, looking pretty docile, hanging out with the herd munching grass, they can actually be quite dangerous. Two metres tall, weighing up to nearly a ton, with a pointy set of horns, and capable of speeds of around 55 kph, a bison charge would be pretty darn savage. Best enjoy the majestic beasts from a safe distance, or maybe even via online slots like Savage Buffalo Spirit Megaways? Joining buffaloes in this game are several other wild animals, a Refilling feature, and free spins with a win multiplier.Savage Buffalo Spirit Megaways is a remake of a BGaming slot released not long before this version came out called Savage Buffalo Spirit. This one has received an expansion via Megaways on licence from Big Time Gaming and mixes up some of the features. Its visuals have been shaken up, though both games are set in the great, wide North American landscape of dust, cacti, and mountains. What's interesting is that despite the huge range of buffalo slots already available, Savage Buffalo Spirit Megaways manages to stand out from the pack, visually. It's not that there is anything hugely special to see, but the particular quality of the artwork is quite somewhat distinct, subtly, and the buffalo itself is white rather than the customary brown.Savage Buffalo Spirit Megaways slot - base gameThe game is played on a grid made up of 6 vertically spinning reels holding 2 to 7 symbols each and a 4-symbol horizontal reel, which sits on top of reels 2, 3, 4, and 5. Since the number of symbols on the reels can change from spin to spin, so does the number of ways to win, going as high as 200,704. With its high volatile math model, RTP comes in three different values depending on the way the game is played, all rather high. When betting 10 p/c to $/€35 per spin, the return value is 97.04%, rising to 97.25% when buying free spins for 90x the bet, dropping to 96.87% when the Chance x2 is activated. The Chance x2 is an ante bet feature that increases the stake by 50%, increasing the chance of hitting free spins.Savage Buffalo Spirit Megaways' paytable is divided between 9-A low-pay royals and high-pay animals such as deer, wolves, cougars, eagles, and bears. Hitting a winning line of 6 royals awards 0.5 to 0.8 times the bet, while a 6 premium symbol win pays out 1 to 10 times the bet. The white buffalo shows up on the wild symbol, appearing on reels 2-5 and the top reel. As well as substituting for any pay symbols, wins including wilds are doubled.Savage Buffalo Spirit Megaways: Slot FeaturesSavage Buffalo Spirit Megaways slot - free spins randomizerSavage Buffalo Spirit Megaways keeps things pretty simple in the features department, replicating some of what occurred in the original game while expanding bits of it. Here, we've got a Refilling feature and free spins.RefillingRefilling is Savage Buffalo Spirit Megaways' name for a cascading/reaction/tumble mechanic. This means that when winning ways are formed, the symbols in the win are removed from the gaming grid. Empty positions are refilled with symbols dropping down from above them, and the refilling process will continue until no new win is created.Free SpinsLanding 3, 4, 5, or 6 scatter symbols in the base game triggers the free spins round and pays 5x, 10x, 20x, or 50x the bet, respectively. Before the round starts, a random number of free spins (5 to 15) and a random multiplier (x2 to x25) are awarded. The multiplier applies to all winning combinations during the round. Should 3 or more scatter symbols hit on a free spin, the feature is retriggered. When retriggered, a random number of free spins and a random multiplier are awarded and summed with the current values. The number of retriggers is not capped, though free spins will end if the win cap is reached.Savage Buffalo Spirit Megaways slot - free spinsSavage Buffalo Spirit Megaways: Slot VerdictSorry to state the obvious, but it doesn't seem like BGaming had incandescent white-hot innovation in mind when it went about designing Savage Buffalo Spirit Megaways. The feature list is relatively short, and what's here doesn't exactly fire the imagination with outrageous possibilities. Quite the opposite, where Savage Buffalo Spirit Megaways delivers relatively basic slot concepts, keeping a safe distance from innovation like a lover of wildlife might keep a safe distance from a herd of buffalo grazing in the fields.That might have sounded negative, but interestingly, Savage Buffalo Spirit Megaways was not a bad game to play. As mentioned, it has a kind of individual look which is hard to pin down and define. Maybe it's the way the reels are presented, or the inclusion of a white buffalo, or how it doesn't look like an Emanuel Gottlieb Leutze painting? Not sure, something's different here. Relatively speaking, that is. Savage Buffalo Spirit Megaways still takes place in the wilderness in a land of popular slot animals, so fans of this style should feel right at home on its range. As for the features, they're alright, nothing special, yet a dependable combination of cascading, free spins and win multiplier have been bolstered by higher-than-usual return stats.If winning potential had been higher than the 6,000x the bet on offer, it wouldn't have hurt Savage Buffalo Spirit Megaways' appeal, though. It's a fairly low figure for a Megaways slot and stands out further when compared to the favourable RTP. All in all, Savage Buffalo Spirit Megaways is not the most memorable or savage buffalo slot out there, though it's not a bad option for those looking for a taste of the wilderness with a simple feature set. Apologies for the game dump, but the good news is players after something a bit bigger are spoiled for choice where options like Big Bad Bison Megaways, Buffalo Mania Megaways, Buffalo Toro, Buffalo Stack' n' Sync, Bison Battle a click or so away.

