            }); LeoVegas Cluster Gems: Slot OverviewOnline casino LeoVegas expands the number of exclusive slots in their Originals series, with the inclusion of a cluster paying grid slot titled, LeoVegas Cluster Gems. LeoVegas has tapped software provider Blueprint Gaming to do so, which is interesting since the studio hasn't released a heck of a lot of these sorts of games. However, Blueprint is far from being novices, having built solid grid slots like Dragon Fall, with more on the way. In LeoVegas Cluster Gems, players collect winning symbols to fill charge meters which unleash modifiers and eventually free drops if enough accrue.This isn't the first time Blueprint Gaming has teamed up with LeoVegas for an exclusive. The previous release was simply titled LeoVegas Megaways, and was built on the game engine on loan from Big Time Gaming. LeoVegas Cluster Gems has a similar look to the previous one, too, using a dazzling blend of reddish, orange, gold colours to make up the blurred background imagery, like someone took a photo of a city, then turned up the contrast and brightness to their highest settings. LeoVegas Cluster Gems isn't as disorientating as LeoVegas Megaways, so you can make out more details such as Las Vegas' Eiffel Tower and Stratosphere Tower. It looks glitzy, ready, and willing for a big night out.Played on a 7x7 sized game grid, the goal is to land winning clusters of at least 5 matching symbols adjacent to each other vertically or horizontally. Winning clusters trigger a cascade feature, which removes them and drops new symbols into the gaps. Cascades continue until no new clusters form. The point is to hit as many consecutive clusters as possible to award features – a standard procedure, grid slot players will be familiar with. A highly volatile slot packing huge potential, LeoVegas Cluster Gems has a theoretical return figure of bang on 95%. Bets can be set from 10 p/c to $/€100 per spin and may be played on any device.A quick run-through of pay symbols before getting to the good stuff. There are 8 regulars, including diamonds, clubs, spades, and heart as the low pays, then three gems and the LeoVegas lion as the four high pays. The largest clusters are formed of 25+ matching symbols and are worth 100 to 1,000 times your stake when made up of the premium symbols. Wilds appear in any position as well, to substitute any regular pay symbol. Wilds pay too, but only if the entire grid is covered in them. The reward for achieving that impressive outcome is 1,000x the bet.LeoVegas Cluster Gems: Slot FeaturesGrid slot players will be well acquainted with the gameplay and features in LeoVegas Cluster Gems. In a nutshell, consecutive clusters fill the Symbol Bank, which drops modifiers at certain levels and eventually triggers free drops. The required levels and their modifiers work like so:Burst – triggered when 20 winning symbols are collected. All symbols on the grid are removed except one gem symbol type and any wilds. New symbols cascade down to fill the grid.Colossal - triggered when 40 winning symbols are collected. A massive symbol is added to the grid in a random position.Wild Times – triggered when 60 winning symbols are collected. Adds a random number of wilds to the game grid.Gem Strike - triggered when 80 winning symbols are collected. This one transforms a random number of gem symbols into the highest paying lion symbol.Cluster FallsCollecting 100 winning symbols awards 10 free cluster falls. During this feature, the number of winning clusters needed to trigger modifiers is reduced, so Burst, Colossal, Wild Times, or Gem Strikes now need just 15, 30, 45, or 60 symbols, respectively. Also, players can retrigger +10 free spins when 75 symbols are collected in the Symbol Bank rather than 100.In addition, free spins have a win multiplier to help build bigger returns. Every time a win occurs in free spins, the multiplier increases by +1. The multiplier does not reset either, so it can continue to grow as the feature progresses.LeoVegas Cluster Gems: Slot VerdictPlayers trawling LeoVegas for a grid slot could do worse than fire up LeoVegas Cluster Gems. It's a competently built game, possessing all the right ingredients for some entertaining cluster paying grid slot action, technically at least. On the other hand, LeoVegas Cluster Gems isn't exactly bursting with innovation and is a little low on x-factor. Personality is largely provided by the LeoVegas lion logo as much as anything else since the rest of the game is pretty standard, though fully functioning. As a smile-inducing side note, LeoVegas has adopted two lions named Bruno and Omar as part of their Leo Initiative to help the majestic creatures.Like the previous game, LeoVegas Megaways, Blueprint has stuck with fairly regular features. At least, the winning symbols leading to modifiers system is a common one. It does tend to work as well here as anywhere else when you can get a good roll-on. It takes some effort to do so, though, and getting to the upper modifiers wasn't easy. Free spins were like gold dust, so be prepared to put in some work to trigger them. Getting there can be worth it, and special things can happen thanks to the lower number of symbols needed to blast modifiers while ratcheting up the progressive multiplier. As to payouts, the game has capped wins at $/€250,000 or 50,000x the bet, which is astronomical for a grid slot, but remember this is a standard clause in many Blueprint games, so it's not necessarily a figure to aim for.As a grid slot, LeoVegas Cluster Gems isn't revolutionary, yet it sufficiently ticks the right boxes. Its features are decent, can go wild under the right conditions, and potential is massive. To sum up, there's nothing preventing LeoVegas Cluster Gems from serving up highly entertaining moments, though a higher RTP might've helped seal the deal.

